  "term": "University of Pennsylvania Smell Identification Test",
  "definition": "The University of Pennsylvania Smell Identification Test is a test of olfactory function, meaning how well a person can identify smells. In this source, lower UPSIT scores indicate poorer smell identification and were associated with dementia with Lewy bodies and Parkinson’s disease dementia compared with Alzheimer’s disease dementia and normal controls.",
